From 0535c06f644cd9282b14661a4821321b4c347a63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rawdanger-recomp <rawdanger-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 01:10:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Raw Danger: AO after the filter and cheaper, option values
 shown, bars in transitions, steps stats

- The AO runs when the game's colour filter ends, not when it starts: under
  the filter's steep brightness curve it came out two or three times as dark,
  black halos round people near walls. Only occluders within about 0.4 m count
  (was 1 m), strength 0.55 (was 0.75). The pass runs once per game pixel and
  lays the result on all its samples (9x less work at 3x resolution).
- The PC rows' spinner values in the game's Options list are drawn by the
  window in the game's font: the game draws a row's sprites from its word
  sheet only, so the words on the background picture never showed.
- The cutscene bars are recognised while they slide in and out (thin, fading):
  'Cutscene bars: OFF' left them in every transition.
- Settings > Debug > Stats: the game steps a second as measured and the
  vblanks a step, also written to the log; PS2_STEPS_LOG prints them every 5 s.
  The Debug steps test puts back the build's own pace (30 / 60 builds).
- Pause in background is off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
